WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:01.690
David.

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:07.279
What do you believe the consequences will
be to the Trump coup, insurrectionist riot?

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:09.429
So it's still too early to know.

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:14.719
But for me, the questions are what will be
the consequences for Trump in the Republican

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:15.719
Party?

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:20.110
I'm going to deal with that in a second segment
because that requires much more time on its

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.110
own.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.560
What will be the consequences for the rioters?

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.290
What will be the consequences for the country?

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.780
And what will be the consequences for Joe
Biden, who's about to be sworn in in the midst

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.410
of absolute insanity?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.920
So for the rioters, it's quite simple.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.800
This now becomes a law enforcement operation.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:41.149
The rioters need to be identified and they
need to be arrested, processed, charged, and

00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:45.679
get them into the justice system and start
working through what what is going on.

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:47.120
Many of them already have.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.469
We've started to see collections of Trump's
mug shots be put together.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:53.730
And these are folks who should be dealt with
seriously.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.519
We already talked about how how would this
have gone differently were this a group of

00:00:58.519 --> 00:01:01.539
black protesters, antifa, black lives matter?

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:03.359
It would have been dramatically different
from the start.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:05.140
Well, we're beyond that now.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:10.160
The question is, how is the justice system
going to deal with these folks?

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.730
And we need to see that process through.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.720
And for the rioters, listen, many of them
are many of them have lost jobs.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.480
Lawmakers have resigned.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.970
We have seen people ostracized by communities.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.490
We've seen all sorts of different things.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.830
You know, a lot of people get their lives
ruined via interactions with police that never

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.580
even should be police interactions here.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.390
Some people are going to get their lives ruined
or at least temporarily ruined because they

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.390
made really bad decisions and did did horrible
things.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:44.970
And so that's that's the path forward for
the rioters, for the country.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.710
I had a segment on Monday about this, and
we're really at a precipice.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.860
We shouldn't understate.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.460
You know, I said this when we were voting
Hillary versus Trump in 2016.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:59.750
Anybody saying Trump, Hillary, it's the same
anybody saying, I don't really know that in

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.190
practical terms, it's much of a difference.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.480
They were wrong and we were talking about
the importance of that decision four years

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.810
ago.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:13.560
And likewise, we are either going to see the
country recognize that even though we're not

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.980
all on the same page politically, that what
happened over the last 10 days goes beyond

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.510
politics and that it cannot be allowed in
any way.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.160
It can't be allowed in our communities at
a microcosm level.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.040
It can't be allowed at the federal level,
at the state level, that this this is not

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.450
valid politics.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.620
And that would be the ideal thing.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.319
And as I said, it's going to require some
Republicans to say, I don't like what Trump

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:39.430
how Trump did his presidency.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:44.319
I am for things like low taxes, low regulation,
et cetera, that are typically more Republican

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:45.319
things.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:47.640
I don't see them in Joe Biden, but Joe Biden
is the president.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.069
And we have to come together and simply respect
that.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.890
It doesn't mean we don't disagree when Joe
Biden does something we don't like.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.080
And that applies to us on the left as well.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.010
That's one path forward.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:02.080
The other path forward is that this type of
riotous insurrection becomes, unfortunately,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.750
more common and considered valid politics
by too many people.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.300
And it's a very dangerous precipice.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:14.430
So what what it means for the country, we
will soon see for Joe Biden, I actually think

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.530
that to some degree this has been good for
Joe Biden.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:19.660
And I want to be really careful.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:26.970
There's never anything good in in in practice
from these riotous coup attempts or what we

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.260
saw.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:35.989
But there is some degree to which I believe
and hope more people than otherwise would

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:41.960
be are better predisposed to the Biden presidency
because it means Trump goes and that that

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:42.989
has to happen.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:48.790
And so I think that Democrats could not possibly
if you had said to Democrats, what can you

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.410
come up with that would happen within two
weeks of Biden's swearing in.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.480
That would best position Biden to get started.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.819
I don't think they could have come up with
anything more beneficial than the Trump is.

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:01.819
Right.

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:02.819
Completely humiliating itself.

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:05.660
Now, I know lots of people liked what the
Trump right did.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.580
There are millions of people who support what
the Trump is right.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.900
Did, but there are many, many Republicans
who don't.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.970
And when it comes to the officials who said,
oh, you know, I'm quitting now, it's too little,

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:17.970
too late.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.480
Chris Christie, Lisa Murkowski, etc..

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.480
It's too little, too late, guys.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.970
You don't get to have your reputations rehabilitated.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:30.911
But for the presumably millions of Trump voters
that are disgusted with what's going on, I

00:04:30.911 --> 00:04:37.490
believe their disgust will better position
Joe Biden for his entry into office.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:38.510
And that's my hope.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.510
Whether it will work out that way or not remains
to be seen.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:05:53.229
Now, let's talk about what this does to Trump
and the Republican Party.

